. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 *
. 
.         * Participants report political leaning preference on a scale from 0-
> 10, where a higher number indicates more left-leaning preference.
.         * So we use DV_H2, which represents political left-right prefences as
>  dependent variable. The original variable was phl0004 but we use the reverse
> d version to have higher values indicating more left leaning which we generat
> ed and named DV_H2.
.         *The independent variable is HasDaughter, a dummy variable coded as 1
>  if the respondent has least one daughter, 0 otherwise.
.         *We use a tobit regression since dependent variable is censored betwe
> en 0 and 10
.         *an additional note is that differently from the PAP we did not have 
> any religiousness measure in this data, hence we have omitted it from control
>  variables.
.         
.         tobit DV_H2 HasDaughter male pglabnet_clean Age YoungestAge Employed_
> p pgisced11_clean pgisced11_p biokids MarriedStatus, ll(0) ul(10) 
note: MarriedStatus omitted because of collinearity.

